SDUSD::setRewardDuration
├── when caller is not owner
│   └── it should revert with OwnableUnauthorizedAccount
└── when caller is owner
    ├── when new duration is less than MIN_REWARD_DURATION
    │   └── it should revert with SDUSDInvalidRewardDuration
    ├── when new duration is greater than MAX_REWARD_DURATION
    │   └── it should revert with SDUSDInvalidRewardDuration
    ├── when new duration equals the current duration
    │   └── it should revert with SDUSDNoStateChange
    ├── when new duration is valid and different
    │   ├── it should update rewardDuration
    │   ├── it should emit RewardDurationUpdated with old and new duration
    │   ├── when the current reward period is active
    │   │   ├── it should not change periodStart or rewardPeriodFinish
    │   │   ├── it should not change rewardsForPeriod, locked rewards, accounted assets, total assets, supply, or exchange rate
    │   │   ├── at the original period midpoint
    │   │   │   └── it should have released half the rewards and increased the exchange rate accordingly
    │   │   └── when the next reward period is notified
    │   │       ├── it should apply the new duration
    │   │       ├── it should not spike the exchange rate at the new period start
    │   │       └── at the new period midpoint
    │   │           └── it should have released half the rewards and increased the exchange rate accordingly
    │   └── when the current reward period has finished
    │       ├── it should not alter the completed reward period state
    │       └── it should apply the new duration to the next notified reward period
    ├── when block timestamp equals rewardPeriodFinish
    │   └── it should allow the update
    ├── when new duration equals MIN_REWARD_DURATION
    │   └── it should allow the update
    └── when new duration equals MAX_REWARD_DURATION
        └── it should allow the update
